CORE
JmlSignalsOnlyKotlin
--function "experiment.JmlSignalsOnlyKotlin.validate:(ZZ)V" --jml-source src/main/kotlin/JmlSignalsOnlyKotlin.kt --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for JML signals_only on Kotlin source.

Mirrors the AWS-Bastion privacy-pipeline idiom: a Kotlin
class declares its own InvalidInputException subtype and a
validation method that throws it under various conditions.
The signals_only contract permits InvalidInputException
(and its subtypes) to escape; JBMC must verify nothing else
can.

Exercises the union of features:
  - JML annotations parsed directly from .kt source
    (jml-kotlin-direct).
  - Instance-method parameter resolution with the implicit
    `this` slot (jml-instance-method).
  - signals_only type-name resolution via the symbol table
    + transitive subclass closure (so a method that throws
    a subclass of the listed type is also accepted).
